{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require schools in England to end the academic year in June",
        "additional_details": "We urge the government to mandate an England-wide academic calendar aligned with Scotland\u2019s model, ending the school year in late June. Climate change has made July heatwaves dangerously intense. Most schools lack air conditioning, leaving pupils and staff trapped in classrooms exceeding 30\u00b0C, which harms health and learning. Shifting to a late-June finish protects children from peak summer heat, prevents disruptive emergency closures, and modernises our education system for a warming world.",
        "background": "Require schools in England to match Scotland\u2019s typical late-June finish. This protects students and staff from dangerous July heatwaves caused by climate change, ensuring they aren't trapped in overheated, uncooled classrooms during peak summer, aiming for a safer, climate-resilient school year.",
